"""Record verified SIM2 source adoption without restamping physical evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=H.parent.parent
def sha(p):return hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()
def main():
 adoption=H/'event-producer-fifo-r1/canonical-adoption-r1/receipt.json'
 a=json.loads(adoption.read_bytes());assert a['status']=='THREE_VERIFIED_DISCONNECTED_SIM2_FIXES_APPLIED_REVERSIBLY'
 assert all(sha(r['path'])==r['after_SHA256'] for r in a['files'])
 docs=[ROOT/'PROJECT_MEMORY.md',ROOT/'reports/ENGINEERING_STATUS.md',H/'README.md']
 backup=H/'project-docs-before-r6';assert not backup.exists();backup.mkdir()
 before={str(p):sha(p) for p in docs}
 for p in docs:(backup/p.name).write_bytes(p.read_bytes())
 def change(p,old,new):
  b=p.read_bytes();x=old.encode();y=new.encode();assert b.count(x)==1,(p,old[:100]);p.write_bytes(b.replace(x,y))
 latest='The verified seven-producer FIFO plus registered RAM bypass and transport alignment correction now maps the full disconnected SIM2 core at 15,805 LUT4 + 2,107 ADD (17,912 total, 1,816 below the coarse T20 limit), 10,441 FF, 63 RAM5K and one multiplier. The original 256-record capacity, seven simultaneous producers, all completed protocol buffers and fitted functions/limits are retained. Strict differential/four-state tests, three semantic mutation controls, the unchanged full runtime suite, 23,596 actual mapped-event-engine vendor-primitive checks and fresh actual eight-/twelve-joint LinuxCNC/HAL/C-driver/SPI/selected-RTL/virtual-plant integrations pass. Vendor models require Verilog-2005 mode in the tested Icarus setup; failed SystemVerilog startup runs and independent reproductions are retained without model edits or internal forcing. These exact three RTL fixes are now applied to canonical disconnected SIM2 with byte backups, guarded rollback and appended provenance. This is no production adoption or physical fit/timing qualification.'
 change(docs[0],
  'Full-core area2 plus a verified transport alignment correction now maps at 18,107 LUTs + 2,107 ADD (20,214 total; still 486 above the coarse T20 screen), with all completed protocol buffers retained. Transport differential and unchanged full-runtime checks pass.',latest)
 change(docs[1],
  'Full-core area2 plus the verified transport alignment correction now maps at 18,107 LUTs + 2,107 ADD (20,214 total; still 486 above the coarse T20 screen). Transport differential and unchanged full-runtime checks pass, with completed protocol buffers retained.',latest)
 change(docs[2],
  'Canonical gateware and all fitted functions/limits remain unchanged; physical wrapper, place/route and timing remain open.',
  'Those qualification runs leave their canonical inputs unchanged at completion. The later verified source adoption below supersedes the current SIM2 implementation; all fitted functions/limits are retained. Physical wrapper, place/route and timing remain open.')
 paragraph='''- `event-producer-fifo-r1/` completes and applies a further behavior-preserving SIM2 implementation correction. Seven fixed producer FIFOs replace the wide bank-write crossbar while the original global 256-entry admission, modulo-256 slot order, modulo-255 nonzero event sequence, seven-events-per-clock capacity, ACK, synchronous prefetch/bypass, clear/reset and payload semantics remain intact. The root differential passes 110,592 seeded boundary cases / 695,104 cycles / 28,164,819 normalized live-record comparisons / 322,187 admitted records. Independent committed-memory/head/wrap/full-capacity/X/Z supplements pass, and three separately compiled timing/tag/capacity mutants fail as required. The unchanged runtime suite passes 1,190 SPI checks, nine event, eleven storage, seven provider checks and 10,000 default-deny cycles. Actual native full-core area2 mapping uses 15,805 LUT4 + 2,107 ADD = 17,912 (1,816 / 9.205% below the conservative 19,728 T20 screen), 10,441 FF, 63 RAM5K and one multiplier. Independent report/CSV/primitive/XML/source review agrees, retaining twelve generators/four encoders. This core map has no physical I/O insertion, wrapper, place/route or timing result.\n\n- `event-producer-fifo-r1/postmap-behavior-r3/` passes 23,596 public-output comparisons against the original event engine using the actual mapped 63-RAM design and installed unmodified vendor primitive models. External traces fill all 256 entries in each producer, exercise full same-producer ACK+append/overflow/drain, forty seven-producer batches, reset/clear and 3,000 binary random clocks. Initial r1/r2 SystemVerilog-mode runs fail at the first reset clock and remain preserved. Independent tiny reproductions show that Icarus SystemVerilog initialization ordering leaves 83 of 175 stable-zero-input vendor LUT masks at their model-initialized zero; the same unmodified models pass all masks/inputs and FF/reset cases in Verilog-2005 mode. The full r3 uses that mode, equivalent Verilog-2005 stimulus syntax, no internal forcing/model edits, and compares every clock. This is initialized binary functional simulation, not postroute timing or physical reset qualification.\n\n- `event-producer-fifo-r1/linuxcnc-pair-r1/` freshly passes actual LinuxCNC task/FREE joint planners/HAL → C driver → serial SPI → the exact selected compiled RTL → independent virtual STEP/DIR plant, first twelve active joints and then eight, all twelve fitted. Its 71-file closures, authored settings, original fixtures and installed rootfs modules remain unchanged/restored, with zero hardware connections and no physical or Cartesian-machining promotion. `canonical-adoption-r1/receipt.json` then applies exactly the tested `cnc3_event_bank.v`, `cnc3_runtime_events.v` and `cnc3_spi_transport_stateful.v` bytes to canonical disconnected SIM2, preserving every other runtime file and appending provenance. Exact four-file backups include the original provenance; guarded `rollback.py` refuses to overwrite later edits. `production_adopted` remains false. No live/adopted board, machine configuration, external IS-1 archive, fabrication release, bitstream or hardware is changed.\n\n'''
 change(docs[2],'## Resource and preservation contract',paragraph+'## Resource and preservation contract')
 summary=H/'event-producer-fifo-r1/README.md';assert not summary.exists()
 summary.write_text('''# Verified disconnected SIM2 resource corrections\n\nThe three verified implementation fixes are applied to the canonical disconnected runtime. This does not adopt a production profile, qualify physical I/O/timing or finish the motherboard.\n\nThe full native T20F256/I4 area2 core map measures **15,805 LUT4 + 2,107 ADD = 17,912**, leaving **1,816** against the conservative 19,728 screen; 10,441 FF, 63 RAM5K and one multiplier are used. All twelve motion generators, four encoders, 256 event records, seven simultaneous event producers and complete protocol buffers remain.\n\nEvidence is separated by scope:\n\n- [Strict original/new queue differential](behavior-receipt.json): 110,592 boundary cases and 28,164,819 logical record comparisons.\n- [Independent functional review and mutation controls](../release-review/producer-fifo-independent-supplement-r1/independent-reviewed-overlay-packet.json).\n- [Unchanged complete SIM2 runtime suite](full-runtime-independent-r1/receipt.json).\n- [Actual native full-core map](native-full-map/receipt.json) and [independent resource/source review](../release-review/producer-full-native-map-independent-r1/receipt.json).\n- [Actual mapped event-engine vendor-primitive simulation](postmap-behavior-r3/receipt.json): 23,596 output checks, every producer filled/drained, resets and binary stress. Failed SystemVerilog-mode startup runs r1/r2 and independent model-language reproductions remain separate. Verilog-2005 mode resolves the reproduced Icarus/vendor-model initialization ordering without model edits, internal forcing or skipped clocks.\n- [Fresh actual eight-/twelve-joint LinuxCNC integration](linuxcnc-pair-r1/receipt.json), explicit disconnected profiles and virtual STEP/DIR plant. Original settings, fixtures and installed modules are preserved/restored.\n- [Canonical adoption and exact backups](canonical-adoption-r1/receipt.json); [guarded rollback](canonical-adoption-r1/rollback.py) restores only if the adopted files still have their expected hashes.\n\nThe actual 135-pin physical boundary is independently classified in [the physical wrapper scope](../release-review/physical-wrapper-scope-r1/scope.md). Real record acquisition is reusable, but authenticated physical provenance, complete I/O/handshake integration, physical implementation and timing remain open. A diagnostic-only image must retain inhibited authority and a distinct identity.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
 result={'status':'EXACT_BYTE_CONTINUATION_UPDATE_AFTER_VERIFIED_CANONICAL_SIM2_ADOPTION','before_SHA256':before,'after_SHA256':{str(p):sha(p) for p in docs},'adoption_receipt_SHA256':sha(adoption),'new_summary_SHA256':sha(summary),'script_SHA256':sha(Path(__file__))}
 (H/'project-docs-update-r6.json').write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2)+'\n');print(json.dumps(result,indent=2))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
